1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,816
Every airplane window has a tiny hole in it.

2
00:00:04,046 --> 00:00:06,725
You've probably sat right next to one

3
00:00:06,745 --> 00:00:08,000
and never noticed.

4
00:00:08,230 --> 00:00:09,804
It's not a crack,

5
00:00:09,824 --> 00:00:11,816
and it's not a defect.

6
00:00:12,046 --> 00:00:13,620
It's there on purpose,

7
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:16,001
and it quietly does two jobs.

8
00:00:16,601 --> 00:00:18,911
Most people assume a plane window

9
00:00:18,931 --> 00:00:20,555
is one thick sheet.

10
00:00:20,785 --> 00:00:22,040
It's actually three.

11
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:24,583
The pane you can touch

12
00:00:24,603 --> 00:00:26,595
is just a scratch shield.

13
00:00:26,825 --> 00:00:29,554
It holds back no pressure at all.

14
00:00:29,784 --> 00:00:32,463
Behind it sit two strong acrylic panes:

15
00:00:32,483 --> 00:00:35,212
a middle one and an outer one.

16
00:00:35,812 --> 00:00:37,017
At cruising altitude,

17
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:39,030
the air outside is thin.

18
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:41,939
The air inside is kept much denser,

19
00:00:41,959 --> 00:00:44,638
so it pushes outward on every window

20
00:00:44,658 --> 00:00:47,018
with hundreds of kilos of force.

21
00:00:47,618 --> 00:00:48,824
That tiny hole

22
00:00:48,844 --> 00:00:50,836
goes through the middle pane.

23
00:00:51,066 --> 00:00:54,114
Cabin air flows into the gap behind it,

24
00:00:54,134 --> 00:00:56,076
so the middle pane feels

25
00:00:56,096 --> 00:00:58,088
equal pressure on both sides.

26
00:00:58,318 --> 00:01:00,997
The outer pane carries the whole load,

27
00:01:01,017 --> 00:01:02,959
and the middle pane waits,

28
00:01:02,979 --> 00:01:04,603
unstressed, as a backup.

29
00:01:05,203 --> 00:01:06,408
Job number two:

30
00:01:06,428 --> 00:01:08,739
that same airflow lets moisture escape,

31
00:01:08,759 --> 00:01:12,225
so the gap stays clear of fog and frost.

32
00:01:12,825 --> 00:01:14,080
One tiny hole.

33
00:01:14,310 --> 00:01:16,671
A spare window and a defogger.

34
00:01:16,901 --> 00:01:18,106
What everyday thing

35
00:01:18,126 --> 00:01:19,750
should we unpack next?
